{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncur=[i for i in json.load(open('state.json'))['interpretations'] if i['id'].startswith('8cff0295')][0]\nkn={k['id']:k for k in json.load(open('state.json'))['knowledge']}\nex=\\\"a20ffdbaf258403c8f0c6a4d4c141e1f\\\"\n\npara=(\\\"Repeat of the same fixed experiment, receipt %s (completed, tests_passed, exit 0): the saved harness and inputs were executed again unchanged, giving a fourth pair of arms at 200 attempts each. Parsed index 0 records the no-delay case state with final_term 400 and max_delay_ms 0, and parsed index 1 its result with inversion_count 1. Parsed index 2 records the jittered case state with final_term 303 and max_delay_ms 2, and parsed index 3 its result with inversion_count 98. The no-delay counts are now 0, 0, 2 and 1 over four independent runs, so the inversion recurs without any added delay and the estimate no longer rests on a single run with two events; the jittered counts are 90, 97, 105 and 98, a band of fifteen events out of four hundred, so added delay remains a large amplifier rather than a precondition. Nothing else about the mechanism changes.\\\" % ex)\n\nlims=list(cur['limitations'])\nlims[0]=(\\\"Two timing modes, 200 attempts each, run four times on one platform: the jittered case produced 90, 97, 105 and then 98 inversions, and the no-delay case produced 0, 0, 2 and then 1. These counts are properties of this harness's delay distribution and scheduler, not a field rate, and the no-delay estimate still rests on three events in eight hundred attempts, so it bounds the order of magnitude rather than the rate.\\\")\n\nces=list(cur['counterevidence'])\nold=ces[0]\nassert old.startswith(\\\"Concurrency alone reaches the inversion, but rarely in this harness at zero delay\\\")\nces[0]=(\\\"Concurrency alone reaches the inversion, but rarely in this harness at zero delay: the four jitter-probe runs recorded 0, 0, 2 and 1 inversions in the 200 no-delay attempts each, and the sweep's zero-delay case recorded 0 in another 200, so three of eight hundred no-delay attempts inverted against ninety to one hundred and five of two hundred with jitter. A rate near one per cent with wide uncertainty is the reading of those counts, so the delay is an amplifier rather than a precondition and the zero-delay counts are small but recurrent.\\\")\n\njoint=cur['joint_history']+(\\\" Receipt %s is a repeat execution of f13b5528eeb44ca99621e36f1c0f1ff0-experiment from its retained inputs, so its four events are the same cases, admissions and assertions as receipts 14a6432138534293b361a796cd32bda8, b89fc1d89b434e8c84a2219073e9a01c and 0ca5ad7d5e8140febbfcf1311e199a4c and differ only in the scheduler's behaviour during that run.\\\" % ex)\n\nk0=kn['830b0f3ff5a14266b056ad4a6d0c877b-knowledge-0']; k1=kn['830b0f3ff5a14266b056ad4a6d0c877b-knowledge-1']\ne0=dict(k0['executions']); e0[ex]=[0,2]\ne1=dict(k1['executions']); e1[ex]=[1,3]\n\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpret receipt %s, a repeat execution of the jitter experiment from its retained inputs. The fourth pair of arms reproduced both readings: an inversion without any added delay and a jittered rate inside the earlier band. The account keeps its violated conclusion and asserted defect claim, updates the counts in the rationale and counterevidence to four runs, and rewrites the limitation so the zero-delay estimate is described as small but recurrent rather than resting on two events.\\\" % ex,\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":k0['id'],\\\"kind\\\":k0['kind'],\\\"statement\\\":k0['statement'],\\\"conditions\\\":k0['conditions'],\\\"source_ids\\\":k0['source_ids'],\\\"executions\\\":e0},\n  {\\\"id\\\":k1['id'],\\\"kind\\\":k1['kind'],\\\"statement\\\":k1['statement'],\\\"conditions\\\":k1['conditions'],\\\"source_ids\\\":k1['source_ids'],\\\"executions\\\":e1},\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"830b0f3ff5a14266b056ad4a6d0c877b-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"f13b5528eeb44ca99621e36f1c0f1ff0-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{ex:[0,1,2,3]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":cur['rationale']+\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\"+para,\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":ces,\n  \\\"limitations\\\":lims,\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":joint,\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":k0['id'],\\\"revision\\\":k0['revision']+1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The transport contract permits the registered heartbeat handler to run outside the main RPC queue, and NetworkTransport dispatches heartbeats that way.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":k1['id'],\\\"revision\\\":k1['revision']+1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"appendEntries decides to raise the term, then writes it unconditionally, and a heartbeat's concurrent execution affects only the term and leader.\\\"},\n  ],\n }],\n}\njson.dump(upd, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\nimport json,jsonschema\ns=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json'))\nd=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'))\njsonschema.validate(d,s);i=d['interpretations'][0]\nprint('schema OK', [(u['revision']) for u in i['knowledge']], len(i['counterevidence']), len(i['limitations']))\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
